body:
Fixes #5817
Clause-②: yes

## What this does

Removes `AppSidebar` from `@object-ui/app-shell`. Nothing in this repository mounted it: `ConsoleLayout` renders `UnifiedSidebar`. objectui#5720 deprecated it after a census; the maintainer has now ruled it can go without waiting for a major release, provided the objectstack console's function is not affected (relayed on the card in comment `5805876559`).

- Deleted `packages/app-shell/src/layout/AppSidebar.tsx` and its own tests (`AppSidebar.derivedAreaVisibility.test.tsx`, `appSidebarSettingsTargets.test.tsx`).
- Removed only the `AppSidebar` export from `layout/index.ts` and from the package entry `src/index.ts`. Nothing else in either barrel moved.
- Shared tests: dropped only the `AppSidebar` case from `systemNavDatasourcesHop`, `systemNavObjectsHop` and `systemNavSettingsTarget`. Every `UnifiedSidebar` case is byte-identical to the base. The two CONTROL cases are code-identical; one comment in each changed from "the two assertions above" to "the assertions above". No shared fixture had to become a local helper: the mocks are shared setup, and their code is unchanged (two of their doc comments were corrected).
- Two source scans read the deleted file by path. Their `AppSidebar` rows were removed: the app-switcher Home row in `homeAffordancesFollowDeclaration-7256.test.ts`, and the `AppSidebar` file in `residue-namespaces-3546.test.tsx`. In the i18n scan, `layout.systemNav.datasources` is now pinned at its surviving `UnifiedSidebar` call site.
- New pin `packages/app-shell/src/__tests__/appSidebarRemoved-5817.test.ts`: the component file is gone, and neither barrel names `AppSidebar` in code (comments masked). It has a control on `UnifiedSidebar`. It follows the shape of `rootLandingHasOneResolver-10042.test.ts`.
- Changeset `.changeset/5817-remove-app-sidebar.md`: `'@object-ui/app-shell': minor` (fixed group, never `major`), stated as breaking in migration terms: use `UnifiedSidebar`, including the gating difference objectui#5720 recorded.
- Pending changeset bodies that this removal made false were corrected. Frontmatter is byte-identical in each: `appsidebar-deprecated-5720.md`, `6335-starred-apps-nav-exclusion.md`, `6507-boot-gate-redirect-splash.md`, `6661-app-launcher-nav-menu-renderers.md`, and `3743-retire-system-hub-card-wall.md` (its "both sidebars" and "sidebar header and user menu" links were `AppSidebar`'s).
- Comments and docs that the deletion made false were corrected, text only. The full list is under M4 below.

⛔ No behaviour change to `UnifiedSidebar`, `ConsoleLayout` or any mounted component. `UnifiedSidebar.tsx` changed in comments only.

## Measurements taken before deleting

**M1, census.**
- In-repo: a comment-masked scan of every tracked JS/TS file (5496 files) finds `AppSidebar` in code only in:
  - its own file and its own tests;
  - the two barrels;
  - the three shared tests;
  - two source scans that read the file by path.
  There is no production import, no lazy import, and no route or registry key.
- objectstack `origin/main` (`a08e059c61`): no import of `AppSidebar`. Its mentions are:
  - CHANGELOGs and a dated audit doc;
  - the liveness ledger `packages/spec/liveness/app.json`;
  - two comments in `packages/spec/src/ui/app.zod.ts`.
  Its `packages/console` is the prebuilt `@object-ui/console` SPA.
- Org-wide code search: `AppSidebar org:objectstack-ai` returned a total count of 52 and 52 items. The known file `packages/app-shell/src/layout/AppSidebar.tsx` was among them, which is the known-hit control. The only hit outside objectui and objectstack is a comment in `objectstack-ai/hotcrm` `src/sales/apps/crm.app.ts`. That comment says its `branding.logo` renders through `AppSidebar.tsx`. It is not an import.
- Built `dist/index.d.ts`, closure plus app-shell `tsc` build:
  - before: the entry's `layout/index.js` re-export list names `AppSidebar`, and `dist/layout/index.d.ts` re-exports it;
  - after: `grep -c AppSidebar` answers 0 in both files.

**M2, the console is not affected.** `ConsoleLayout` mounts `UnifiedSidebar` as its sidebar and `AppHeader` (with `AppSwitcher`) as its navbar. The M1 scan finds no route, lazy import or registry key that reaches `AppSidebar`. The following are green:
- the console build (`tsc`, `vite build`, `build:plugin`);
- its post-build gates;
- the whole app-shell and console suites (listed under Verification).

**M5, i18n.** `check:i18n-keys` is green. The sweep that reads the other direction, `check:i18n-dead-keys`, is report-only and wired into no workflow. After the removal it adds ten keys with no call site:
- CONFIRMED: `layout.appSwitcher.{addApp, appsAvailable, editApp, editNavigation, home, manageAllApps, noAppsConfigured, systemConsole}` and `user.settings`;
- NEEDS-REVIEW: `sidebar.searchNavigation`.
No gate asks for their removal, so the packs are untouched.

**M4, prose.** Comments were edited only where the deletion made them false. Each edit is text only.
- Touched:
  - `ExpressionProvider.tsx` (the JSDoc example now wraps `UnifiedSidebar`);
  - `console/AppContent.tsx` (the add-app clause);
  - `ConsoleShell.tsx` and `bootRedirectCoverage.test.tsx` (the `SystemRedirect` rationale keeps `SettingsView` only);
  - `StarredApps.tsx`;
  - `FavoritesProvider.tsx`;
  - `UnifiedSidebar.tsx` (four pointers to `AppSidebar`);
  - `ActionResultDialog.tsx` and its test;
  - `nav-menu-renderer.tsx` (the same three providers are now named as `UnifiedSidebar`'s, which wires them identically);
  - `ExpressionProvider.visibleFaultDiagnostic.test.ts` (the `hasActionHandler: false` wiring is now credited to `AppSchemaRenderer` without `onAction`, because `UnifiedSidebar` wires `true`);
  - `UnifiedSidebar.derivedAreaVisibility.test.tsx`;
  - `navItemVisibleEvaluated.test.tsx`;
  - `AppContent.noAppsCta.test.tsx`;
  - `AppContent.pseudoRouteSegments.test.tsx`;
  - auth: `AuthProvider.tsx`, `UserMenu.tsx` and `signOut-client-cache-purge-5198.test.tsx`;
  - `useRecordEditable.principalScope.test.tsx` (it quotes the `AuthProvider` sentence, kept in step);
  - `MePermissionsProvider.capabilitiesReported.test.tsx`;
  - `app-creation-types.test.ts`;
  - apps/console: `AppContent.tsx` (two present-tense "both sidebars" clauses), `AppManagementPage.tsx` (the call-shape example is now `AppSwitcher`), and `AppContent.systemHubRoutes.test.tsx` (the zero-app branch note);
  - `content/docs/guide/console-architecture.md`.
- Left, with reason:
  - every `CHANGELOG.md` is published history;
  - `ROADMAP.md` entries are completed history;
  - `docs/audits/2026-06-ui-testability.md` is a dated audit;
  - the `AppSidebar.systemFallbackNavigation` bullet in apps/console `AppContent.tsx` is an explicitly dated reading ("when this redirect landed");
  - the past-tense "What was wrong" history in the three shared tests is kept, with a removal note;
  - the header counts in `residue-namespaces-3546.test.tsx` were measured at that slice's branch point;
  - the header of `homeAffordancesFollowDeclaration-7256.test.ts` describes the original defect, so a note was added beside the table instead;
  - the "both sidebars" mentions in `QuickActions.tsx`, `QuickActions.settingsTarget.test.tsx`, `AppContent.noAppsCta.test.tsx` (the objectui#3590 retarget) and `AppContent.pseudoRouteSegments.test.tsx` narrate what those issues changed at the time;
  - "Both sidebar entries" in `AppContent.noAppComponentRoutes.test.tsx` means the two nav entries, and it is still true.

## Verification

Suites ran on the tree of `4a4e58d9e`. The final head `0bec5284e` adds one comment-only edit to `AppContent.systemHubRoutes.test.tsx`; that file and the new pin were re-run green on `0bec5284e`, as were the cheap gates.

- Builds:
  - `pnpm --filter '@object-ui/app-shell^...' build`, then app-shell `tsc` build (dist completeness: 934 emitted files verified): exit 0.
  - Console build (`tsc`, `vite build`, `build:plugin`): exit 0. It first needed six console-only dependencies built (`plugin-gantt`, `plugin-map`, `plugin-markdown`, `plugin-timeline`, `plugin-tree`, `test-support`); on the first try `tsc` could not resolve them, which was a missing prerequisite, not a failure.
  - The built console bundle contains no `AppSidebar` string.
- Post-build gates: `check:eager-closure`, `check:eager-locale-catalogues` and `check:sdui-registration-pins` all exit 0.
- Type checks: `type-check` for `@object-ui/app-shell`, `@object-ui/i18n` and `@object-ui/console` exits 0. Counted with `--listFiles`, the app-shell test tsconfig includes the new pin and the edited scans.
- Suites:
  - app-shell, `pnpm exec vitest run packages/app-shell/` in 6 shards: 797 files (1 skipped), 8062 tests passed, 9 skipped, every shard exit 0;
  - console, `pnpm exec vitest run apps/console/`: 117 files, 1288 tests passed;
  - `packages/i18n/`, `packages/auth/` and the i18n, unreferenced-sources, line-citation and skills-paths script tests: 102 files, 1824 tests passed;
  - the 17 edited test files: 179 tests passed.
- Gates at `0bec5284e`, all exit 0:
  - `check-changeset-presence`, `check-changeset-no-major`, `check-changeset-fixed`;
  - `check:new-line-citations` (0 new citations);
  - `check:control-bytes`;
  - `check:changeset-claims` (report-only; each of the six flagged paragraphs was read, and none is falsified by this change);
  - `check:i18n-keys`, `check:test-path-roots`;
  - `governed` (NOT GOVERNED).
- Other gates, all exit 0 at `4a4e58d9e`:
  - `check:i18n-drift`, `check:unreferenced-sources`, `check:phantom-deps`, `check:unused-deps`, `check:self-import`, `check:esm-specifiers`, `check:pending-changeset-literals`;
  - `check:readme-exports`, green once the unrelated `cli` and `plugin-ai` were built (the first run stopped on their missing type entries);
  - docs: links, fences, component types, spec symbols;
  - `check-changeset-overwrite` (report-only; it lists the five corrected changesets with unchanged declarations).
- Lint on the 31 touched TS files: 0 errors. The 110 warnings are the same 110 that the base versions of those 30 files produce; the new pin has 0. (Count note from the seat: the surface has 31 modified TS files plus the new pin, so one modified file was outside this local run. The repo-wide `Lint` check-run is green on this head.)
- No `api-extractor` config or `.d.ts` snapshot gate exists in this repo.
- Reverse proof, on committed `HEAD`, via `ablation-replace.mjs` with the trap restore:
  - The barrel export was restored in both barrels. The mutation landed (anchor count 1 to 0 in each; `grep -c AppSidebar` answered 1 in each barrel).
  - The pin went red: "Tests 2 failed | 2 passed", with the two barrel cases red and the file-absence and control cases green.
  - Restore was proven by blob equal to `HEAD` and an empty `git diff HEAD`. The pin then read 4 passed.
  - The first attempt was refused by the tool: its anchor was contained in its own replacement, so nothing was measured. It was re-run with a non-overlapping anchor.
- NOT MEASURED:
  - repo-wide `pnpm test` and E2E, reason: CI owns them;
  - full suites of `permissions`, `plugin-detail` and `types`, reason: their edits are test comments only, and the edited files ran green;
  - repo-wide lint, reason: CI.

## Acceptance notes

**objectstack liveness ledger, `packages/spec/liveness/app.json`.** One line for each row that cites `AppSidebar` as read evidence. The citations are pinned at `@940ba24`, so they still resolve as addresses; what goes stale is their standing as evidence of a live reader.

- `label`: live readers are `AppSwitcher` (`resolveKeyedI18nLabel(activeApp.label, t)` for the pill, and each row of the switcher list), `ConsoleLayout` (`appLabel` feeding `AppHeader` and the `AppShell` branding `title`), and `HomeAppsStrip` (launcher tiles).
- `description`: the live reader is apps/console `AppManagementPage` (the system/apps list line and search filter). The ledger's "rendered under the active app's title" presentation has no successor: no mounted chrome shows the active app's description. `AppCard` reads it but has no in-repo mount point.
- `icon`: live readers are `AppSwitcher` (`getIcon(app.icon)` on each switcher row) and `HomeAppsStrip` (`getIcon(app.icon)`).
- `branding`: the row covers logo, primaryColor, accentColor and favicon.
  - `primaryColor` is live: `ConsoleLayout` hands `activeApp.branding.primaryColor` to `AppShell`, and `useAppShellBranding` (layout `AppShell.tsx`) sets the brand CSS variables.
  - `branding.logo` has no other runtime reader. Only authoring surfaces read it: plugin-designer `EditAppPage` (prefill) and the `BrandingEditor` / `AppCreationWizard` previews. `AppSchemaRenderer` reads the top-level `logo`, not `branding.logo`.
- `active`: live readers are `AppSwitcher` and `UnifiedSidebar` (the `a.active !== false` filter and active-app lookup) and `filterActiveApps` (utils `appRoute.ts`, used by `HomePage` and `app-launcher-renderer`). The row's note also cites an `AppSidebar` comment.
- `hidden`: live readers are `AppSwitcher` and `UnifiedSidebar` (`a.hidden !== true`) and `filterActiveApps`.
- `navigation[].id`: live readers are `UnifiedSidebar` `useNavOrder` (reorder persistence by id), `useNavPins` (`pinnedNavIds`), `NavigationRenderer` (the sortable id and pin toggles) and `nav-menu-renderer` (row keys and the active row).
- `navigation[].visible`: the live reader is `UnifiedSidebar` `evalVis`, which is `evaluateVisibility(expr, evaluator)` handed to `NavigationRenderer` and to `hasVisibleNavigationItems`; `nav-menu-renderer` wires it the same way. `NavigationRenderer` is already cited on the row.
- `areas[].id`: the live reader is `UnifiedSidebar` (`activeAreaId` election and the switcher `key`).
- `areas[].label`: the live reader is `UnifiedSidebar` (`resolveInlineI18nLabel(area.label, language)`).
- `areas[].icon`: the live reader is `UnifiedSidebar` (`getIcon(area.icon)`).
- `areas[].navigation`: the live reader is `UnifiedSidebar` (`activeArea?.navigation` and `hasVisibleNavigationItems(area.navigation, …)`). `AppSchemaRenderer` is already cited on the row.
- File `_note`: it lists "app-shell AppSidebar/ConsoleLayout/ContextSelectors" among objectui's consumers.
- Related objectstack prose, not ledger rows: `packages/spec/src/ui/app.zod.ts` names `AppSidebar` in the `recordId` template-variable note and in the `AREA_ORDER_RETIRED` note. `UnifiedSidebar` also iterates `areas` in the order they are authored.

Other notes:
- `branding.logo` is authored but no longer rendered by anything that ships. The console never mounted its only reader, so this gap predates this PR. Authors still write it: plugin-designer's `BrandingEditor`, the published 17.6.0 CHANGELOG ("To show a logo, set it on the app schema's `branding.logo` instead") and hotcrm's `crm.app.ts` all do. The seat owns the ledger card (`5805876559`).
- Overlap: seat 2's objectui#7483 may add an `ObjectView` type export to `src/index.ts`. This PR removes one line in the layout-chrome export block of that file. The lines are disjoint; a conflict is resolved by merge commit.
- Observation, not filed: `console/home/AppCard.tsx` is exported but not mounted in-repo.

